==English==
{{slim-wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dewk-}}
From {{der|en|la|abductiō|t=robbing; abduction}}, from {{m|la|abdūcō|t=take or lead away}}, from {{m|la|ab|t=away}} + {{m|la|dūcō|t=to lead}}.<ref>{{R:CDOE|page=2}}</ref> Equivalent to {{suffix|en|abduct|ion}}.
* {{sense|physiology}} From {{bor|en|fr|-}}, from {{der|en|la|abductus}}.
* Compare {{cog|fr|abduction}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əbˈdʌk.ʃn̩/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-abduction.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/æbˈdʌk.ʃn̩/|/æbˈdək.ʃn̩/|/əbˈdək.ʃn̩/|a=US}}
* {{sense|anatomy sense}} {{q|for emphasis and disambiguation from {{m|en|adduction}}}} {{IPA|en|/ˈeɪ.ˈbiː.dʌk.ʃn̩/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# Leading away; a [[carry]]ing away. {{defdate|from early 17<sup>th</sup> century.}}<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5|page=3}}</ref>
# {{senseid|en|Q308502}} {{lb|en|anatomy}} The act of [[abduce|abducing]] or [[abduct]]ing; a [[draw]]ing apart; the [[movement]] which [[separate]]s a [[limb]] or other part from the [[axis]], or middle line, of the body. {{defdate|from mid-17<sup>th</sup> century.}}<ref name=SOED/>
#* '''2013''', Jain, MD, MSPH; Wilcox, PT; Katz, MD, MS; Higgins, MD, "Clinical Examination of the Rotator Cuff", [[w:American_Academy_of_Physical_Medicine_and_Rehabilitation#Publications|''PM&R Journal'']], retrieved from  [https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3826176 PubMed Central] on 21 Jan 2018.
#*: '''Abduction''' is performed by asking the patient to raise the arm at the side as high as they can with the examiner stabilizing the scapula by holding it down.
# {{lb|en|logic}} A [[syllogism]] or form of [[argument]] in which the [[major]] premise is [[evident]], but the minor is only [[probable]]. {{defdate|from late 17<sup>th</sup> century.}}<ref name=SOED/>
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Ronnie Cann; Ruth Kempson; Lutz Marten|title=The Dynamics of Language, an Introduction|page=256|passage=The significance of such a step is that it is not morphologically triggered: it is a step of '''abduction''', and what is required here is a meta-level process of reasoning.}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} The [[wrongful]], and usually [[forcible]], [[carry off|carrying off]] of a human being. {{defdate|from mid-18<sup>th</sup> century.}}<ref name=SOED/>
#: {{co|en|the '''abduction''' of a child}}
# {{lb|en|ufology}} [[alien abduction|Alien abduction]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2010|author=w:Monte Dwyer|title=Red in the Centre: Through a Crooked Lens|publisher=Monyer Pty Ltd|page=122|passage=But fear of '''abduction''' never stopped a good ufologist.}}

